                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="OnmnXBfdHe-ymCt0516s-22" value="LLM&lt;div&gt;- input tokens (Y1)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- output tokens (Y2)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- llm custom cost (Y)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;-llm total token*&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=card;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="490" y="650" width="130" height="130" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="six7A13i6lqTk6c3Tc23-105" value="Circle of non-computation" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="130" y="-260" width="130" height="70" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="six7A13i6lqTk6c3Tc23-107" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Token equivalent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- not 30$ simple, because everyone else speaks the language of tokens&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- Providers always give their pricing in /M tokens, therefore, purely for the sake of easing our computation, we can say the token equivalent of 30$ is 30$*1M/$ = 30 M&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- For this token equivalent to truly reflect usage, input tokens and output tokens must contribute toward it in the right proportions (i.e. weighing them according to their relative prices given by the provider)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- e.g. model:&amp;nbsp;gpt x&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;input price: 0.25&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;output price: 1.25&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- Say, Frank has consumed 25$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- that's 25M tokens&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;if&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- (without proportions): input tokens + output tokes = 25M&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;::this fails because at the level of the provider, the cost is split depending on who is an input token and who is an output token, so 25$ is almost certainly not the exact price registered by the provider::&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;21.25M output, 3.75M input&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;provider calculates:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;21.25*1.25+3.75*0.25 = 27.5$ (for which our token equivalent is 27.5M)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;- (with proportions): input tokens*weight +output tokens*weight = 25M&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;::This works::&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;...&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="790" y="-584" width="490" height="190" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="six7A13i6lqTk6c3Tc23-110" value="redis" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=28.36365023526264;fillStyle=dashed;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="630" y="160" width="170" height="160" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
